{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049100-best-praxis","id":1049100,"title":"Best Praxis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-14T19:35:35-08:00","id":1049100,"title":"Best Praxis","content":"Praxis can be really nice. Not only are they a way to recover willpower by criting on three successes but you can either pull a point of mana out of them or gain a favorable condition (not limited by the spell duration) that will give you an arcane beat when it resolves. That's a pretty good way to get some arcane xp. So what are the best spells to turn into praxis:<br /> <br /> Spells that you are going to cast all the time at low potency. Unveiling spells are particularly nice is you're likely to have at least two reaches available. <br /> So:<br /> Speak with Dead (Death 1), <br /> Web of Life (Life 1), <br /> Find the Balance (matter 2, best with matter 3 and using a mana for extended duration), <br /> Mental Scan (Mind 1, best with at least mind 2 -- note this spell is withstood, possibly making in non-ideal), <br /> Pierce Deception (prime 1), <br /> Correspondence (Space 1), <br /> Locate Object (Space 1, though perhaps less than useful as most scenes are not going to give a chance to cast it to find your keys), <br /> Divination (time 1).<br /> <br /> Spells where using a crit to avoid withstand is better than using a rote and paying the dice to overcome the withstand:<br /> Command Spirit (Spirit 2), <br /> Psychic Domination (Mind 2, though the number of reaches involved can make this questionable).<br /> <br /> Spells that might come up a bit less often but are cast at a low potency. <br /> Knit (errata) and Mend (errata). Knit is healing at least three lethal per casting (base of 1 plus two free pushes) and mend is healing eight lethal (base of one plus three free pushes). It's an excellent chance to crit with a big out of combat dice pool casting on each teammate after a fight. <br /> Invisibility (Forces 2), Actually, I can see this getting used all the time.<br /> Call lightning (forces 3 -- actually you probably don't get to use this enough to justify it, but getting a beat and a favorable conditions adds insult to the substantial injury you just caused someone).<br /> <br /> Spells that allow you to break things horribly if you crit.<br /> Exceptional Luck (Forces 2). This might be the only spell that you want as both a praxis and a rote. If you crit the casting roll you can not only take a favorable condition that gives you an arcane beat, but add a number of favorable conditions that give you regular beats when resolved. Oh yeah, with a crazy amount of reach your inspired condition can let your next spell crit on three successes as well. Basically a way to churn beats.<br /> <br /> Platonic Form: Costs 1+ mana. With a crit all mana is refunded and you gain one extra mana. Basically a way to straight up summon mana.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12994-steveintexas","name":"SteveInTexas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T22:48:56-08:00","id":1049154,"title":"","content":"I like Diviniation (Time 1). You can ask a simple question like &quot;will my next spell succeed?&quot; and gain the Steadfast condition for you Exeptional Success.<br /> Resolving Steadfast lets you get a guaranteed success on spells you would normally have a single die or even chance die on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 02-15-2017, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T00:55:59-08:00","id":1049182,"title":"","content":"I would think that Matter 2: Shaping, would be extremely useful for making Environmental tilts, or weakening armor or possibly even harming an enemy with their own armor, perhaps by shaping their kevlar into a hood that melds to their face preventing them from breathing, or seeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T01:35:32-08:00","id":1049189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SteveInTexas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049100-best-praxis#post1049100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptional Luck (Forces 2). This might be the only spell that you want as both a praxis and a rote. If you crit the casting roll you can not only take a favorable condition that gives you an arcane beat, but add a number of favorable conditions that give you regular beats when resolved. Oh yeah, with a crazy amount of reach your inspired condition can let your next spell crit on three successes as well. Basically a way to churn beats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exceptional Luck (Fate 2) not (Forces 2)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T04:24:32-08:00","id":1049218,"title":"","content":"All the Compelling, Knowing, and Unveiling Practices would smoothe regular life so much that everything would look <i>trivial</i>. Small wonder why mages tend to see themselves as superior to Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T17:53:15-07:00","id":1525047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SteveInTexas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049100-best-praxis#post1049100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spells that allow you to break things horribly if you crit.<br /> Exceptional Luck (Forces 2). This might be the only spell that you want as both a praxis and a rote.<b> If you crit the casting roll you can not only take a favorable condition that gives you an arcane beat, but add a number of favorable conditions that give you regular beats when resolved</b>. Oh yeah, with a crazy amount of reach your inspired condition can let your next spell crit on three successes as well. Basically a way to churn beats.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thread necromancy but this is the best place to ask the question.<br /> <br /> As both the exceptional success Condition and the Conditions from the spell succeding come from spellcasting, does it mean that only a single Arcane beat can be earned per scene? No regular beats for those conditions, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcane Beats p. 83 Mage Awakening 2ed Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022<b>Any time you resolve a Condition resulting from spellcasting, Paradox, or a magical effect, take an Arcane Beat<br /> instead of a normal one.</b> Letting a spell causing a Condition expire does not count as resolving it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T20:04:05-07:00","id":1525052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049100-best-praxis?p=1525047#post1525047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As both the exceptional success Condition and the Conditions from the spell succeding come from spellcasting, does it mean that only a single Arcane beat can be earned per scene? No regular beats for those conditions, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>See &quot;Conditions and Tilts&quot; and the related sidebar on page 126 of the corebook. The favorable Conditions don't grant regular Beats because they're favorable Conditions created by magic, not because that would be getting more than one Beat for a single casting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T06:14:21-08:00","id":1525068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049100-best-praxis?p=1525052#post1525052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See &quot;Conditions and Tilts&quot; and the related sidebar on page 126 of the corebook. The favorable Conditions don't grant regular Beats because they're favorable Conditions created by magic, not because that would be getting more than one Beat for a single casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant in the example that I bolded from the OP, assuming an extraordinary success both conditions (the one from being an extraordinary sucess, and whatever boon you get from the spell itself as per the Boons section on Fate magic p.134) are Arcane beat granting.<br /> <br /> The poster seems to think that the extraordinary sucess Conditions grants Arcane beats when solved but the Boon granted conditions are regular beats, I am posting that even if you get them to grant beats (for an extraordinary success), all Conditions would grant Arcane beats since all come from spellcasting.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T06:24:37-08:00","id":1525069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1049100-best-praxis?p=1525068#post1525068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The poster seems to think that the extraordinary sucess Conditions grants Arcane beats when solved but the Boon granted conditions are regular beats, I am posting that even if you get them to grant beats (for an extraordinary success), all Conditions would grant Arcane beats since all come from spellcasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that would be correct, with the additional caveats that the Conditions in question would not be able to grant more than one Arcane Beat per scene, the end of the spell's Duration would remove any Conditions that hadn't been resolved without providing Beats, and the boon would have to grant beneficial Conditions that were different Condition or separate instances of the same Condition applying to different and specific things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T18:30:21-08:00","id":1525103,"title":"","content":"<i>Coaxing the Spirits:</i> The universal remote control.<br /> <br /> <i>Influence Electricity:</i> control cellphones, hotwire a car, disable any security system, shut down all the lights, hack the computer, its has a lot of great applications.<br /> <br /> <i>Serendipity:</i> Allows you to rely on your specialty skills to tackle an important objective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}